   "translation": "Simplified characters are the Chinese characters that were simplified in the course of character simplification; they stand against traditional characters (orthodox characters). In different settings they are often popularly called 简体字, 简笔字 or 俗体字, or, with contempt, 残体字 'crippled characters'. Since most Chinese characters were in fact never simplified, those have the standard name 传承字 'inherited characters' in mainland China.",
   "note": "The script of every modern card is 简化字; the script of your Analects cards is 繁体字."
